Hello,

I am trying to build a phylogenetic tree of ~1000 nodes with msa, phangorn and ggtree packages.

I aligned my sequences with msa:msaMuscle(), then run some phangorn package code get optim.pml fit object and then plot it with ggtree. At the line:

phangorn <- treeio::phyPML(fit, type="ml")

I get an error saying:

phangorn <- treeio::phyPML(fit.tmp, type="ml")
Error in getSubsLabel(fasta, label[parent[i]], label[i], translate, removeGap) :
  seqA should have equal length to seqB
In addition: Warning messages:
1: In FUN(newX[, i], ...) : ambiguous found...

2: In FUN(newX[, i], ...) : ambiguous found...

I also tried with ggtree::phyPML() or just phyPML() functions. Any reason why is this not working? Code and sessionInfo are added below

library(phangorn)
library(msa)
library(ggtree)

fastaAligned62 <- msa::msaMuscle(fastaRefined62, verbose=TRUE)

uniprot.refined <- as.phyDat(fastaAligned62)
rm(fastaAligned62)

names(uniprot.refined) <- homologySummary62[1:length(uniprot.refined),]$SequenceFullName

dm <- dist.ml <http://dist.ml>(uniprot.refined, model="JTT")
tree <- NJ(dm)

cat('Testing all models ...\n')
(mt <- modelTest(uniprot.refined, model="all", multicore=TRUE))
env <- attr(mt, "env")
fitStart <- eval(get(mt$Model[which.min(mt$BIC)], env), env)
fitNJ <- pml(tree, uniprot.refined, model=fitStart$model, k=4, inv=.2)
fit <- optim.pml(fitNJ, rearrangement = "stochastic",
                     optInv=TRUE, optGamma=TRUE)
fit
phangorn <- treeio::phyPML(fit, type="ml")

tiff("HomologyTree.tiff", width = 6400, height = 6400, units = "px", res = 800)

ggtree(phangorn) + geom_text(aes(x=branch, label=AA_subs, vjust=-.5))

dev.off()

